  "coverage": [
    "The editor's live registry exposes declarative regex definitions, extension lookup, metadata and rules through direct calls.",
    "Independent registries support empty creation, native defaults, replacement and checked cleanup.",
    "Replacing an active definition refreshes tokens on the unchanged document at the next paint; replacing another definition does not dirty the editor.",
    "Failed native registration preserves the old definition and XRT live heap at 12 consecutive allocation budgets.",
    "View release detaches observation, editor close expires the view, and native or xlang cross-thread access is checked.",
    "Windows/Linux generated calls, JIT, dynamic/static AOT, and the bounded GUI example use the same validated package cohort."
  ],
  "costs": [
    "Generated C initializes one native descriptor and allocates one temporary record array for each nonempty group.",
    "Input strings undergo C-string admission, native storage copies definitions, and query results copy borrowed strings.",
    "Native regex compilation remains part of tokenization when the cache is cold. No language callback runs for a declarative rule."
  ],
